/*
Authored by Triplis

Additional credits:
- LtLi0n: Help with a Typescript/Javascript bug
- Moonbow: Contribution to UI design
- Moonbow, FurbyMask: early feedback and testing
- SomethingRoom script: Some pieces are lifted from it for AeR-like scaffolding

v1.1.5 changelog:
- Imitate: Have the AI gen Example Chats from existing chat context
  - Under AR Diaries > squiggly icon page > click Imitate to gen
  - Add to Example Chats to save the gen to the Contact's example chats and delete it after
  - Or delete it if you don't like it
  - Note: These entries will do nothing until they are added to example chats. Will probably work better with lots of existing chat to gen off of. The general idea here is, you made a Contact and they developed a unique voice beyond strict description; you want to maintain that through examples in the card, in a way that can be carried into other chats.
- Process: Have the AI gen a brief emotion-based reflection
  - Under AR Diaries > smile icon page > click Process to gen
  - These are similar to Diaries but focus on emotional impact specifically
- Emotional Modes: Optional extra emotion-related influence on Contact behavior
  - Enable under AR Global > Use Emotional Modes
  - How it works?
    - It looks for recent emotions in chat and can match them to a little extra prompting toward specific emotional states, if enough matching emotions are present
    - If Track Real Time is on and an hour+ has passed since generating, a random emotional state is picked for the next response, prompted on the idea of them being affected by emotions outside of the chat. This aims to add more of a sense of simulated life outside the chat and increase the chance of time away / resume breaking the AI out of pre-existing emotional patterns, as opposed to endlessly repeating them.
- Card Brains: import/export brains separately from the card itself
  - Sometimes you may have brain entries you made for one Contact and you want them in another Contact. Now you can export the brain entries for Contact A and then import them into Contact B.

TODO:
- FORUM:
  - Possibly allow user to forum reply (as a Contact persona that isn't OP or as a name they specify or as a random name)
  - Possibly have a chance for random name repliers to show up in the replies again somehow
*/

function getRandomNameFull()
{
  return getRandomNameThey() + " " + getRandomNameSurname();
}

function getRandomNameThey()
{
  const gender = api.v1.random.int(0, 1);
  if (gender === 0){
    return getRandomNameMale();
  }
  else if (gender === 1){
    return getRandomNameFemale();
  }
}

function getRandomNameMale() : string
{
  const min = 0;
  const max = NAMES_LIST_MALE.length - 1;
  const index = api.v1.random.int(min, max);
  return NAMES_LIST_MALE[index];
}

function getRandomNameFemale() : string
{
  const min = 0;
  const max = NAMES_LIST_FEMALE.length - 1;
  const index = api.v1.random.int(min, max);
  return NAMES_LIST_FEMALE[index];
}

function getRandomNameSurname() : string
{
  const min = 0;
  const max = NAMES_LIST_SURNAMES.length - 1;
  const index = api.v1.random.int(min, max);
  return NAMES_LIST_SURNAMES[index];
}

